+# Southbag inject-only worker: broker contract (candidate proposal)
+
+This document is the proposed interface between the root broker (OS side,
+owned by the OS worker) and the Kevin capitalisation worker (this source
+candidate). It is a proposal for review, not a shipped contract. No physical
+device grant, unit activation, or package pin is authorized by this document
+or by any candidate constructor. If anything here conflicts with broker-side
+realities, the broker side proposes the change; do not let two incompatible
+contracts evolve independently.
+
+## 1. Spawn-time grants (environment + inherited FDs)
+
+The broker spawns the worker with a scrubbed environment containing exactly:
+
+| Variable | Meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| `SOUTHBAG_WORKER_GENERATION` | Decimal u64 > 0. Binds every grant and the shared terminal gate to one broker generation. A restart gets a new generation; stale components from an older generation are denied admission. |
+| `SOUTHBAG_INPUT_GRANTS` | Comma-separated `fd=token` entries, one per broker-approved physical input device. The fd is an already-open evdev device fd inherited across exec, opened `O_RDONLY|O_NONBLOCK|O_CLOEXEC` by the broker (validated at adoption via `F_GETFL`; a blocking grant is denied because the read loop drains until `EWOULDBLOCK`). The token is the broker's opaque device identity (`[A-Za-z0-9._:-]+`). fds and tokens each unique. |
+| `SOUTHBAG_MONITOR_FD` | One fd (pipe or eventfd) owned by the broker's topology monitor. ANY readiness or hangup means monitor gap/loss. The worker never reads payload from it. |
+| `SOUTHBAG_UINPUT_FD` | One already-open `/dev/uinput` fd, opened `O_WRONLY|O_NONBLOCK|O_CLOEXEC` by the broker (validated at adoption via `F_GETFL`; checked writes fail closed with `EWOULDBLOCK`, never hang). The worker configures and creates the virtual output device on it and destroys it on exit. The worker binds the device's sysfs phys to `southbag:<generation>` (the exact `SOUTHBAG_WORKER_GENERATION` value) via `UI_SET_PHYS` before `UI_DEV_CREATE`; the launcher proves the device is this worker generation's exact output by monitoring for BOTH the exact name and the expected phys plus a single new sysfs path, rejecting any preexisting match or second path. The bare name contract is unchanged; the phys is the binding. |
+
+Worker behavior:
+
+- Missing, malformed, aliased, or unopen fds, generation 0, duplicate fds or
+  tokens: the worker refuses to start (exit before any device or output
+  setup). There is no fallback to scanning `/dev/input` or opening
+  `/dev/uinput` by path.
+- Each input fd is validated after exec: open fd, evdev keyboard/mouse
+  capability (EVIOCGBIT), resolvable name. Any failure denies the grant.
+- Synthetic-output exclusion: a granted fd reporting the virtual output
+  device name (`Espanso virtual device`, single source of truth
+  `espanso_info::SOUTHBAG_UINPUT_DEVICE_NAME`) is denied. This is defense in
+  depth; the broker remains responsible for never granting the synthetic
+  device as input.
+- Batch preflight: the detector validates the WHOLE epoll batch before any
+  device read or input callback - shared terminal state, monitor readiness
+  or hangup anywhere in the batch (dominates; marked first), EPOLLERR/
+  EPOLLHUP or an unresolvable tag on any entry, and liveness of every
+  granted fd. A batch that observes loss admits zero callbacks, even when
+  input readiness precedes the loss entry. Terminal state is also rechecked
+  BETWEEN raw-event callbacks, since the engine consumes them concurrently.
+- The detector re-checks each granted fd's liveness after every epoll wake
+  (valid fd, capability still present, name resolvable and not synthetic).
+  With inherited fds the fd IS the device; removal surfaces as read/poll
+  failure, which is terminal.
+
+## 2. Shared terminal gate (one object per generation)
+
+The worker creates exactly one `TerminalGate` bound to
+`SOUTHBAG_WORKER_GENERATION`, shared by detector, funnel, engine, and
+injector. Stop reasons: `InputUncertain`, `OutputUncertain`, `MonitorLost`,
+`ExplicitStop`, `PolicyFault`. First reason wins; no reset, rearm, or resume.
+
+Terminal inputs (fail closed, marked at the point of loss):
+
+- Input: EPOLLERR/EPOLLHUP on any granted fd, any read error (including
+  ENODEV), EOF, truncated input records, SYN_DROPPED, detector initialization
+  failure, detector thread exit for any reason (backstop guard), liveness
+  re-check failure.
+- Topology/monitor: any readiness or hangup on `SOUTHBAG_MONITOR_FD`;
+  missing monitor.
+- Output: any checked-write (uinput) failure, including short writes.
+- Policy: lock poison, admission-counter overflow, generation mismatch.
+
+Observed stop closes admission permanently, wakes every listener (including
+a blocked empty select), and discards backlog: the engine checks terminal
+state before dequeue, after dequeue, after processing, and before each
+output event. Logical rechecks are not atomic with an output syscall; a
+write already in flight is outside this guarantee (section 4).
+
+## 3. What the worker does NOT do
+
+- No local IPC socket: no trigger, toggle, expansion, or shutdown commands.
+- No clipboard, compositor, notification, or desktop app-info probing.
+- No dynamic renderer extensions (shell, script, date, form, ...).
+- No built-in debug/search/restart triggers.
+- Exactly the pinned static rule: trigger `kevin` (plain substring, no word
+  boundary, no case propagation) replaced with `Kevin`, plain-text key
+  injection. At most one copy; the dormant state is zero rules. NOTE: probe
+  fixtures used `:kevin`; the exact trigger spelling must be reconciled with
+  the reviewed product rule before activation.
+- No capability raising (no DAC override), no device discovery, no hotplug
+  watcher of its own, no per-device DAC decisions.
+
+## 4. Broker obligations (outside this candidate)
+
+- Own physical device identity: which event nodes are the approved
+  keyboards, and proof the fd passed is that device.
+- Own the topology monitor: detect add/remove/change of the approved set and
+  signal monitor loss over `SOUTHBAG_MONITOR_FD`; never signal spuriously.
+- Own bounded stop completion: admission drained is not unit/FD/driver
+  cleanup. Stop requested, admissions drained, unit empty, input/output FDs
+  closed, grants revoked, and compositor/modifier state restored are distinct
+  states; the broker verifies each, including a blocked in-flight syscall.
+- Own unit lifecycle: start only with all gates verified, stop on terminal
+  exit, no auto-restart of a terminal generation (worker exits with a
+  non-restart error on `TerminalFailure`).
+
+## 5. Known limits (unchanged by this candidate)
+
+- A logical status check is not atomic with an output syscall.
+- The gate does not select or trust devices; tokens carry no provenance.
+- Hotplug between epoll wakes is observed at the next wake, not instantly;
+  the broker monitor covers the async case.
+- The guard is not a watchdog; it converts observed loss into inhibition.
